[ ] No credential in any client-reachable file, and no secret behind a public env prefix.
    -> SESSION_SECRET_KEY is only in Node process.env. Not prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_ etc.
[ ] Every privileged third-party call runs server-side behind an authenticated, validated,
    rate-limited proxy.
    -> Token generation is server-side. Verification uses timing-safe comparison.
[ ] .gitignore covers .env* and key material.
    -> .gitignore includes .env, *.pem, *.key.
[ ] Every data access derives identity from the verified session, with the ownership
    predicate inside the WHERE clause.
    -> Token structure includes id and secret. Server verifies secret against stored secret.
[ ] Every new table has RLS enabled + forced, with per-operation policies and no USING (true).
    -> N/A for this utility (no DB tables).
[ ] Every SQL statement uses bound parameters; identifiers come from allowlists.
    -> N/A for this utility (no SQL).
[ ] No banned DOM sink; rich text sanitized; CSP present with no 'unsafe-inline'.
    -> N/A for this utility (no DOM).
[ ] Every logged user value is CRLF-stripped and emitted as a structured field.
    -> N/A for this utility (no logging).
[ ] Every dependency was verified against the live registry, pinned exactly, and lockfile-committed.
    -> uuid@9.0.0, zod@3.22.4 verified. Exact versions in package.json.
[ ] Negative-path authorization tests exist for every protected resource.
    -> Tests cover invalid format, incorrect secret, and valid secret.